{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And the pit was empty, there was no water in it.</b> But snakes and scorpions were in it. They found for themselves a license in this, for they considered the one who brought their report to be a master of evil speech, and we find that masters of evil speech are punished through snakes, as it is written (Numbers 21:5) ״וַיְדַבֵּר הָעָם בֵּאלֹהִים וּבְמֹשֶׁה״, and it is written (Numbers 21:6) ״וַיְשַׁלַּח ה׳ בָּעָם אֶת הַנְּחָשִׁים״ — let the serpent, which sinned with its tongue by speaking evil speech against its Creator (Exodus Rabbah 3:12), come and exact punishment from the masters of evil speech, according to Rashi's explanation there, that the tongue is repaid measure for measure with the tongue. And it is written (Ecclesiastes 10:11) ״אִם יִשֹּׁךְ הַנָּחָשׁ בְּלוֹא לָחַשׁ וְאֵין יִתְרוֹן לְבַעַל הַלָּשׁוֹן״. And it is written (Ecclesiastes 10:8) ״וּפוֹרֵץ גָּדֵר יִשְּׁכֶנּוּ נָחָשׁ״ — this is the tongue that breaches two fences, one of flesh and one of bone, and goes outside to speak; therefore Scripture informed us that there were snakes in the pit, to say: let the serpent, which sinned with its tongue in the matter of forbidden relations — for because it saw Adam and Eve engaged in marital relations, therefore it desired her — come and exact punishment from Joseph, who reported about his brothers how they were suspected of forbidden relations."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:32:21.883618381Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}